11. SECURITY RULES — COMPREHENSIVE
============================================================

--- Authentication ---
  - Passwords: NEVER plain text — SHA256 + unique salt per user
  - Tokens and session data: SecureStorage only
  - Session timeout: auto-logout after inactivity (configurable)
  - Failed login attempts: lock account after 5 consecutive failures

--- Data isolation (most critical rule) ---
  EVERY database query that fetches user data MUST include
  a WHERE ErabiltzaileId = [currentUserId] filter.
  An employee MUST NEVER be able to see another employee's tickets,
  name, amount, or any personal data — not through the UI,
  not through API calls, not through any workaround.
  Validate this server-side too, not only in the ViewModel.

--- Role enforcement ---
  - Role stored in SecureStorage after login, verified on every navigation
  - Admin routes: check role BEFORE loading any data (fail fast)
  - If role check fails: redirect to login, clear session, show error
  - Never trust role data coming from the UI — always re-verify from storage

--- Database file protection (SQLite) ---
  - Enable SQLite encryption using SQLCipher (SQLite-net-pcl extension)
    so the .db file is unreadable if copied to a PC
  - Encryption key: derived from a device-specific value + app secret
    (never hardcoded as a plain string)
  - Store the derived key in SecureStorage, regenerate if not found
  - NEVER store the raw encryption key in source code or config files
  - On Turso: data is encrypted in transit (TLS) and at rest by default

--- Network ---
  - All HTTP requests use HTTPS only — no HTTP allowed
  - Pin SSL certificate for production API (if custom backend)
  - Never log request bodies, tokens, or user data to console/files
  - All API responses validated before use (never trust raw server data)

--- Photo security ---
  - Server-side: photos accessible only via authenticated URLs (signed URLs
    or token-protected endpoints) — never public/unauthenticated access
  - Client-side: cached photos stored in app private cache directory only

--- Input sanitization ---
  - Sanitize all user text inputs before DB insert
  - Always use parameterized queries — never string concatenation in SQL
  - Validate amount: must be positive number, max 2 decimal places
  - Validate date: must not be in the future

--- Audit log ---
  - Every approve/reject action logged in AuditoretzaLoga
  - Log: ErabiltzaileId, Ekintza, DataOrdua, IP_Helbidea, affected ticket Id
  - Logs are read-only — no delete or update operations on AuditoretzaLoga

--- Environment Variables & Secrets ---
  - External credentials (Turso URL/token, Cloudinary cloud name, upload preset, API keys) MUST be stored in a .env file (or secure pipeline secrets for release builds).
  - The .env file MUST be explicitly listed in .gitignore.
  - NEVER write real database URLs, JWT tokens, or API keys in this .cursorrules file or any .cs file.

