14. ABSOLUTE PROHIBITIONS
============================================================

  - NEVER write business logic in code-behind
  - NEVER instantiate services with new() — use DI
  - NEVER store passwords in plain text
  - NEVER query the database on the UI thread
  - NEVER use English for variable/method/class names (see §4 exceptions)
  - NEVER leave empty catch blocks
  - NEVER use a single generic catch without specific ones above it
  - NEVER use Thread.Sleep — use Task.Delay
  - NEVER put DB queries in ViewModel constructors — use OnAppearing/LoadAsync
  - NEVER modify files outside the agreed scope without asking
  - NEVER invent file or folder names not in §2
  - NEVER proceed with large changes without presenting a plan first
  - NEVER store photos as blobs in SQLite — store URL/path only (see §9)
  - NEVER allow a user to access another user's data (see §11)
  - NEVER show admin UI elements to employees or vice versa (see §6)
  - NEVER hardcode encryption keys or secrets in source code
  - NEVER hardcode Turso credentials (URL/Token) or Cloudinary secrets — always read from .env or secure config
  - NEVER generate decorative comments, ASCII art, or structural borders (like =================== or -------------------) in the code. Keep comments plain, minimal, and professional using standard // or /* */ without extra symbols.

