15. CHANGE PROTOCOL — MANDATORY BEFORE EVERY ACTION
============================================================

STEP 1 — READ RULES
  Read this entire file before doing anything.
  Do not skip sections. This step is required for every change.

STEP 2 — PLAN
  State explicitly:
    a) Which files you will modify
    b) What exact change in each file
    c) Why (problem it solves)
    d) Which files you will NOT touch

STEP 3 — CONFIRM
  Large or multi-file changes: present plan, wait for approval.
  Small single-file changes: state plan inline, proceed if unambiguous.

STEP 4 — EXECUTE
  Make only the changes stated in Step 2.
  If something unexpected appears: STOP and report. Never improvise.

STEP 5 — REPORT
  Summarize: what changed, what did not change, follow-up needed.

